      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2011 Tianjin Lung Cancer Institute and Blackwell Publishing Asia Pty. Ltd.",
        "AbstractText": "We report an extremely unique histologically proven case of an isolated primary pleural granulocytic sarcoma (chloroma) in a 44-year-old woman who had sustained complete remission for 14 years after being treated for a Hodgkin's lymphoma. There was no history of myelogenous leukemia, which typically precedes chloroma. The prognosis was dismal as the patient died 2 weeks after diagnosis."
      },
